			<item>
				<title>Model Temperature and Sampling</title>
				<link>http://localhost:1313/ai-as-technology/temperature-and-sampling/</link>
				<pubDate>Wed, 25 Nov 2026 21:20:44 +1100</pubDate>
				<guid>http://localhost:1313/ai-as-technology/temperature-and-sampling/</guid>
				<description>&lt;p&gt;A model predicts one token at a time, and each token is a probability spread over many possible tokens. Temperature and sampling decide how the next token is picked from the spread.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;ol&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;A model gives probability for every possible next token. It does not output one word. For the next tojen it produces ranked spread, for example&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ol&gt;&#xA;&lt;table&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&lt;thead&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;tr&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;th&gt;&lt;/th&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;th&gt;&lt;/th&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&lt;/thead&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&lt;tbody&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;tr&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;td style=&#34;text-align: center&#34;&gt;cut off&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;td style=&#34;text-align: center&#34;&gt;55%&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;tr&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;td style=&#34;text-align: center&#34;&gt;vendor&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;td style=&#34;text-align: center&#34;&gt;25%&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;tr&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;td style=&#34;text-align: center&#34;&gt;network&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;td style=&#34;text-align: center&#34;&gt;15%&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;tr&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;td style=&#34;text-align: center&#34;&gt;unknown&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;td style=&#34;text-align: center&#34;&gt;5%&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&lt;/tbody&gt;&#xA;&lt;/table&gt;&#xA;&lt;ol start=&#34;2&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Sampling picks one token from the spread. The tool rolls a weighted die. A 55% is chosen about 55 times in 100 runs, not everytime&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Temperature reshapes the spread before the roll.&#xA;Low temperature makes the most likely token much more dominant.&#xA;High temperature flattens the spread so unlikely tokens get picked more often&#xA;At temperature 0, the tool always takes the top token&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ol&gt;</description>
			</item>
			<item>
				<title>What is an embedding?</title>
				<link>http://localhost:1313/ai-as-technology/embeddings/</link>
				<pubDate>Wed, 25 Nov 2026 21:20:44 +1100</pubDate>
				<guid>http://localhost:1313/ai-as-technology/embeddings/</guid>
				<description>&lt;p&gt;An embedding is a way of turning text (or images, audio, etc.)into a list of numbers, called a vector, so that things with similar meanings end up with similar numbers.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;For example, &amp;ldquo;I forgot my login credentials&amp;rdquo; and &amp;ldquo;How do I reset my password&amp;rdquo;  share almost no words but their embeddings point in nearly the same direction. A keyword search would miss the match, while embedding search finds it.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h3 id=&#34;why-it-matters&#34;&gt;Why it matters?&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Enbeddings power:&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
			<item>
				<title>Language Models</title>
				<link>http://localhost:1313/ai-as-technology/llm-models/</link>
				<pubDate>Sun, 22 Nov 2026 21:20:44 +1100</pubDate>
				<guid>http://localhost:1313/ai-as-technology/llm-models/</guid>
				<description>&lt;h1 id=&#34;llm-vs-slm&#34;&gt;LLM vs SLM&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;h1 id=&#34;what-is-large-language-model&#34;&gt;What is Large Language Model?&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Large Language Model (LLMs) are statistical models of language. They extract patterns and relationships in massive amounts of text and build mathematical representation of how words relate to each other.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h1 id=&#34;frontier-models&#34;&gt;Frontier Models&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;A Frontier Model is a highly capable, general-purpose AI model at or near the leading edge of AI development. Unlike narrower models designed for specific tasks, frontier models can perform a broad range of complex tasks and generally require substantial data and computing resources to develop. As AI technology advances, what qualifies as a frontier model may shift.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
